From 3770100a393ec63298636d118799155b679a628e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 22:52:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 198/307] fix: RSM near-plane pancaking erased the volume
 content at larger cascade scales

Root cause of the cascade-scale energy loss / displaced bounce hunt
(diagnosed with the debug-8 alignment probes): caster membership is an
AABB overlap test against the swept box, so huge nodes (terrain hills,
merged tree patches) become members while most of their geometry lies
sun-ward of the sweep. With the near plane sitting exactly at the sweep
distance, that overhanging geometry got pancaked onto the near plane
and its silhouette erased everything behind it from the RSM - solid
canopy/hill blobs blotting out the hangar and the ground. The blotted
area grows with r_LPVCascadeScale (a bigger swept box overlaps more of
those nodes), which produced the ~1/scale energy loss, the seemingly
displaced bounce, and the increased wall leaking (roof texels eaten by
a blob lose their geometry-volume presence).

The clip range is now decoupled from the collection sweep (>= 2500m):
membership and draw calls stay identical, members just can no longer
pancake. D16 precision over the enlarged range stays at centimeter
level, far below the cell size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tu9cj9ax1mqCV93HVfCfpW
---
 Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/ShadowCache.cpp | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/ShadowCache.cpp b/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/ShadowCache.cpp
index 2a0007ee..e9ebe56f 100644
--- a/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/ShadowCache.cpp
+++ b/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/ShadowCache.cpp
@@ -394,6 +394,16 @@ void ShadowCacheGenerator::InitLPVRsmFrustum(ShadowMapFrustumPtr& pFr, int nLod,
 	// Everything between the sun and the volume can throw light into it, so extend the near plane.
 	const float casterRange = max(Get3DEngine()->m_fSunClipPlaneRange, 2.0f * halfExtent);
 
+	// The CLIP range has to be much larger than the caster collection sweep: collection is by AABB
+	// overlap, so huge nodes (terrain hills, merged tree patches) become members even though most
+	// of their geometry lies sun-ward of the sweep - with the near plane at the sweep distance that
+	// geometry gets pancaked onto the near plane and its silhouette ERASES everything behind it
+	// from the RSM (observed as solid canopy/hill blobs blotting out the hangar and the ground, and
+	// growing with r_LPVCascadeScale because the bigger swept box overlaps more of those nodes).
+	// D16 precision over the enlarged range stays at centimeter level, which is far below the cell
+	// size.
+	const float clipRange = max(casterRange, 2500.0f);
+
 	// Virtual light distance instead of the astronomic distance to the real sun light origin: with
 	// fDist ~1e6 the resulting projection (near ~= far ~= 1e6, FOV ~0.01 deg) is so ill conditioned
 	// that the fp32 inversion in CLPVStage::UpdateFrameParameters degenerates and the VPLs land at
@@ -431,7 +441,7 @@ void ShadowCacheGenerator::InitLPVRsmFrustum(ShadowMapFrustumPtr& pFr, int nLod,
 	// cascade, so the RSM depth encoding stays identical to the cascade based path.
 	pFr->fFOV = (float)RAD2DEG(atan_tpl(halfWidth / max(fDist, 1.0f))) * 2.0f;
 	pFr->fProjRatio = 1.0f;
-	pFr->fNearDist = fDist - halfDepth - casterRange;
+	pFr->fNearDist = fDist - halfDepth - clipRange;
 	pFr->fFarDist = fDist + halfDepth;
 	pFr->fRendNear = pFr->fNearDist;
 
